\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Let $S=\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, with $n\geq2$, and let $P_1,\ldots,P_s$ be general distinct points of $\mathbb P^{n-1}$. Write $\mathfrak p_j$ for their homogeneous prime ideals, $I=\bigcap_{j=1}^s\mathfrak p_j$, and, for $m\geq1$,
\[I^{(m)}=\bigcap_{j=1}^s\mathfrak p_j^m,\qquad I^m=\underbrace{I\cdots I}_{m\text{ factors}}.
\]
For a graded ideal $J$, use $\operatorname{Hilb}_J(t)=\sum_{e\geq0}\dim_{\mathbb C}J_e\,t^e$.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Determine, for every $n,s,m$, the entire series
\[\operatorname{Hilb}_{I^{(m)}}(t)-\operatorname{Hilb}_{I^m}(t)
 =\sum_{e\geq0}\dim_{\mathbb C}(I^{(m)}/I^m)_e\,t^e.
\] \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.01692}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine in every degree how symbolic powers of an ideal of general points differ from its ordinary powers.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{description}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 1500016 (AMR-014-0016). CC BY 4.0. \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] R. Fröberg, S. Lundqvist, A. Oneto and B. Shapiro, \emph{Algebraic Stories from One and from the Other Pockets}, arXiv:1801.01692 (2018), §3.2, Problem K. \url{https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.01692}.
\end{description}
